{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.MathlibExt.PosSemidefTraceZero","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.PosSemidefTraceZero","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.LinearAlgebra.Matrix.PosDef","lean:module:Mathlib.LinearAlgebra.Matrix.Spectrum","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic","lean:module:QOU.MathlibExt.PosSemidefDiagZero","lean:module:QOU.MathlibExt.FrobeniusInnerProduct"],"declarations":5,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.PosSemidefTraceZero.Matrix.PosSemidef.kernel_containment_of_product_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.PosSemidefTraceZero.Matrix.PosSemidef.kernel_containment_of_product_zero","kind":"theorem","line":244,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/PosSemidefTraceZero.lean#L244-L257","doc":"**Kernel containment from complementary slackness.**\nIf `S · Φ = 0`, every column of `Φ` lies in the kernel of `S`.\nCombined with primal feasibility (`Φ` PSD with prescribed trace\nconstraints) this pins `Φ` down to a low-dimensional subspace\n— the linear-algebraic core of SDP-optimum uniqueness. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.PosSemidefTraceZero.Matrix.PosSemidef.complementary_slackness","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.PosSemidefTraceZero.Matrix.PosSemidef.complementary_slackness","kind":"theorem","line":229,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/PosSemidefTraceZero.lean#L229-L242","doc":"**SDP complementary slackness** (matrix form).  If the dual\nslack `S := T - Σ_i y_i A_i` is PSD, the primal `Φ` is PSD,\nand the duality-gap measure `tr(S · Φ) = 0`, then `S · Φ = 0`.\nThis is the bridge identity used in SDP-uniqueness arguments. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.PosSemidefTraceZero.Matrix.PosSemidef.trace_mul_eq_zero_iff_mul_eq_zero_diagonal","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.PosSemidefTraceZero.Matrix.PosSemidef.trace_mul_eq_zero_iff_mul_eq_zero_diagonal","kind":"theorem","line":193,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/PosSemidefTraceZero.lean#L193-L227","doc":"**Diagonal sub-case of cone self-polarity.**\n\nFor diagonal PSD matrices `A = diag(a)`, `B = diag(b)` with\n`a, b : Fin n → ℝ` non-negative, `tr(A · B) = 0 ↔ A · B = 0`.\n\nPROOF: `A · B = diag(a_i * b_i)`, so `tr(A · B) = Σ a_i b_i`.\nEach summand is non-negative; sum zero ⟹ each summand zero\n⟹ each `a_i b_i = 0` ⟹ diagonal entries of `A · B` are zero\n⟹ `A · B = 0` (off-diagonal of a diagonal matrix is zero).\n\nThis is the foundation for the general spectral argument:\ndiagonalise `A = U D Uᵀ`, then the general case reduces to\nthis diagonal case via cyclicity of trace. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.PosSemidefTraceZero.Matrix.PosSemidef.trace_mul_eq_zero_iff_mul_eq_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.PosSemidefTraceZero.Matrix.PosSemidef.trace_mul_eq_zero_iff_mul_eq_zero","kind":"theorem","line":64,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/PosSemidefTraceZero.lean#L64-L191","doc":"**Cone self-polarity for PSD matrices** (real case).  For\nPSD matrices `A, B : Matrix (Fin n) (Fin n) ℝ`,\n`tr(A · B) = 0 ↔ A · B = 0`.  The forward direction is the\nnon-trivial half (the reverse is `tr 0 = 0`).\n\nPROOF SKETCH (forward):\n1. Diagonalise `A = U D U^T` with `U` orthogonal, `D` diagonal\n   non-negative (via `Matrix.PosSemidef.eigenvectorMatrix`).\n2. `tr(A B) = tr(U D U^T B) = tr(D U^T B U)` (cyclic).\n3. `U^T B U` is PSD (orthogonal-similar to PSD `B`).\n4. `tr(D U^T B U) = Σ_i D_ii · (U^T B U)_ii`, each summand ≥ 0.\n5. Sum = 0 ⟹ each summand = 0 ⟹ on the support of `D`, the\n   diagonal of `U^T B U` is zero ⟹ (PSD diagonal-zero ⟹\n   row+col zero) `(U^T B U)_{ij} = 0` whenever `D_ii > 0`.\n6. Therefore `D · U^T B U = 0`, hence `A · B = U D (U^T B U) U^T\n   = 0`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.PosSemidefTraceZero.Matrix.PosSemidef.diag_nonneg","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.PosSemidefTraceZero.Matrix.PosSemidef.diag_nonneg","kind":"theorem","line":50,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/PosSemidefTraceZero.lean#L50-L62","doc":"**PSD diagonal entries are non-negative**.  Mathlib's standard\nfact, restated here for direct use. ","signatureChunk":0}]}